2Ti 1:1 , Paul's love to Timothy, and the unfeigned faith which was in Timothy himself, his mother, and grandmother;
2Ti 1:6 , He is exhorted to stir up the gift of God which was in him;
2Ti 1:8 , to be stedfast and patient in persecution;
2Ti 1:13 , and to persist in the form and truth of that doctrine which he had learned of him;
2Ti 1:15 , Phygellus and Hermogenes, and such like, are noted, and Onesiphorus is highly commended.
